    "summary": "Painting on board; a woman outdoors, performing in front of a toi moko (tattooed preserved head) on a stake.  She wears a hei tiki (neck pendant), a kahu huruhuru (feather cloak), and a skirt (appears to be a korowai cloak type); she performs in front of a wharenui (meeting house), with carved amo (upright support) and maihi (sloping panel) visible; other people gathered around watching.  1900s.\r\nPaint on board.",
